nisha (DevEx): Flagging a nasty onboarding hit — quickstart paginator sample can trigger a token+retry stampede and exhaust table-level quotas in under 30s. Repro attached.

nisha (DevEx): Short repro steps:
1) Start quickstart with PAGE_SIZE=40 and MAX_CONCURRENCY=6
2) Set auth TTL to 2s (local dev flag)
3) Load 20 pages quickly (simulate infinite scroll)
4) Some requests get 429s while auth refresh races; client retries whole page loop and fires duplicate requests

jun (QA): Confirmed locally. Spinner hung and network tab shows duplicate calls for the same page id. Bulk 429s then a flood of successes (same items returned multiple times).

nisha (DevEx): From the quickstart code: fetchPages spawns multiple page workers and each worker has its own retry around the page fetch. Code excerpt:
```
async function fetchPages(cursor) {
  const workers = Array.from({length: CONCURRENCY}, (_,i) => (async () => {
    let cur = cursor;
    while (cur) {
      for (let t=0;t<MAX_ATTEMPTS;t++) {
        try {
          const res = await client.list({cursor: cur, limit: PAGE_SIZE});
          cur = res.next;
          break;
        } catch (err) {
          if (err.code === 'UNAUTH') { await auth.refresh(); continue; }
          if (err.code === 'RATE_LIMIT') { await sleep(500 * 2**t); continue; }
          throw err;
        }
      }
    }
  })());
  await Promise.all(workers);
}
```

sam (SDK): This pattern retries at worker/page level — if auth.refresh() rotates the token other inflight retries aren't gated, so they retry with new token and duplicate the page fetch. Without an idempotency key or an inflight guard the server receives N nearly identical requests.

leo (Platform): We also noticed the SDK HTTP client currently exposes a retryPolicy but the sample app overrides it with its own loops. Two issues: (1) request-level backoff + idempotency headers not used, (2) no per-cursor mutex so multiple workers can process the same cursor when retries overlap.

jun (QA): I recorded network trace: 6 workers, page=5 requested 6x, server responded 429 to 4 of them, then token rotated, and the remaining 2 retries all returned 200 with identical payloads. Client then appended duplicates to UI.

ratelimiter-bot: [event] quota:table:items sample-quickstart exceeded soft limit 1m requests/min for project:devex-sample at 2026-03-21T11:05:23Z

ci-bot: flaky test alert: paginator/quickstart.test failed in CI twice; reproduces in docker with AUTH_TTL=2s.

sam (SDK): Proposed fixes (short-term):
- move retries into the HTTP layer (requestWithRetry) so only the single HTTP call retries, not the whole page loop
- add idempotency header "X-Idempotency-Key" for list calls (generate from cursor+limit)
- provide an in-memory inflight map keyed by cursor to ensure only one inflight request per cursor (per process)
- expose maxConcurrentPages in quickstart and default to 2

leo (Platform): Additional platform-side mitigation: when token rotation is in progress, SDK should delay non-essential retries for a short window (100-300ms) to allow a single refreshed token to serve inflight requests rather than causing stampedes. Also add jitter to backoff.

nisha (DevEx): UX note: for onboarding it would be great if quickstart logs a warning when it detects repeated 429s and suggests lowering concurrency or increasing token TTL. New users hit this and think the platform is broken.

jun (QA): I can add a test harness that simulates token expiry + 429s to catch regressions.

sam (SDK): Implementation plan: 1) add requestWithRetry in SDK and opt-in idempotency for list endpoints (internal only), 2) update quickstart to remove per-page retry loops and use SDK retry, 3) add per-cursor inflight mutex in quickstart sample and expose CONCURRENCY knob, 4) add docs blurb. I'll open PRs today.

nisha (DevEx): Thanks — please also include a small note in the quickstart README about the token TTL env var and a link to the SDK retry docs. I'll shepherd the docs change.

sam (SDK): One more thought: we should avoid global blocking during auth refresh — instead SDK should broadcast a refresh-in-progress event and let requestWithRetry await refresh resolution for callers that need it, with a bounded wait. Prevents head-of-line blocking.

leo (Platform): Agreed. We'll also add a Prometheus metric for "client_retries_due_to_auth" so we can alert when this pattern emerges in customer apps.

jun (QA): Verified quick local patch: moving retry to HTTP wrapper + inflight map removed duplicate calls and reduced rate-limit events from 90/min to 6/min. UI no longer shows duplicates or permanent spinner.

nisha (DevEx): Great, thanks everyone. Leaving this thread as the incident note and onboarding doc pointer. :party_parrot:
